# 35. Real-World Example: Private SSH Key

SSH private keys are sensitive.

A private key should not normally be readable by everyone.

Example:

```bash
chmod 600 ~/.ssh/id_rsa
```

This gives:

```text
Owner  → read + write
Group  → no access
Others → no access
```

If permissions are too open, SSH may refuse to use the private key.

